Z||000006||Haze_Performance||03-30-2001||03:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jch82:<BR><B>I liked the conversion to the little round taillights. That looks sweet!<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Daytonak.JPG">  <P>Josh   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Where can I get the backup light at? I called PISA, and they said I can only get all red or 3 red + 1 amber...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Thanks<BR>Haze  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">     </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A>||||reg||5
Z||000007||Phil||03-30-2001||04:24 PM||||The yellow car is mine with the Pisa setup. I made the backup lights(required in RI) I took the red lens and cut the center out and glued in a section from a clear lens that I found at an RV supply store. I didn't use the Pisa sockets(too $$$), I made my own by taking a piece of sheet metal and putting in some of those $2 sockets and pop reviting the assembly onto the tail light panel. The lenses are Harley Davidson turn signals. BTW they're sequential too.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">    <BR>SC 3800<P><p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||03-30-2001||05:04 PM||||my easy mod was Mar-Hyde plastic dye. it just looks black but the lites are still bright at night and even with stock bulbs you can read the PONTIAC just fine... <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst-rear-tag.jpg"> ||||reg||1
